codex
The live code confirms two important adaptation boundaries. Schema-v6 has no implementation stub yet—`skillspec.py` still caps support at `{1…5}` and actively tests schema 6 as unsupported. The transaction root is similarly greenfield: one coarse `.lock` wraps CLI install/update/upgrade/GC, while project writes, consumer registry updates, and GC remain incremental. I’m now checking the accepted rc.5 schema cases and lifecycle vector so the producer plans name every positive/negative case rather than inventing behavior.
